d counterparty context to the quarter."},{"period_end":"2025-10-31","narrative":"The filing reported RPO and disclosed new cloud-infrastructure and AI-service commitments. The quarter therefore included substantial future infrastructure obligations alongside reported operating losses."},{"period_end":"2026-01-31","narrative":"The filing reported RPO dependent on customer consumption and disclosed committed cloud, purchase, and lease obligations. Related-party vendor and customer arrangements, investments, and the subsequent Observe acquisition provide additional context for the quarter’s economic exposure."},{"period_end":"2026-04-30","narrative":"The filing reported RPO and disclosed a revised cloud agreement with substantial annual minimum spending. The quarter also included future lease commitments and a conditional acquisition agreement, indicating significant forward obligations beyond reported operating results."}],"prose":{"overview":"Revenue grew 50% per year, faster than expenses at 35% per year. The backlog equals 1.8x one year of revenue, giving the $9.2 billion backlog meaningful scale against $5.0 billion of trailing-year revenue.","debt":"Total committed money is $1.4 billion, including $490 million for leases. That adds lease commitments beyond reported debt and captures other committed spending.","wall":"The next five years carry $9.3 billion of obligations, while only $56 million of revenue is promised for that period. Another $217 million of obligations falls after year five without a stated revenue schedule.","flags_note":"The filings describe a circular-financing relationship involving Observe, which was an investor, customer, and vendor before Snowflake acquired it. They also describe an increase from a $1.0 billion aggregate cloud infrastructure commitment with no minimum purchase commitment to a $6.0 billion cumulative minimum spend, plus a $34.0 million gain on remeasurement of a previously held equity interest presented as revenue."}}